      }
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "raw-definition",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-raw-image-format",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-c499a5131665"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-c499a5131665",
          "exact": "A camera raw image file is a file that contains unprocessed data straight from a digital camera. Such data can later be changed into a photo, either within a digital camera itself or by usage of external tools. Raw files are so named because they are not yet processed, and contain large amounts of potentially redundant data."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-c499a5131665",
          "subject": "camera raw image file",
          "predicate": "contains",
          "object": "unprocessed data straight from the camera; so named because not yet processed; contains large amounts of potentially redundant data"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002",
        "ARC-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "evidence-c499a5131665 [0,326) 逐句覆盖 claim 三要素：'contains unprocessed data straight from a digital camera' 对应\"包含相机直出未处理数据\"；'Raw files are so named because they are not yet processed' 对应\"因尚未处理而得名\"；'contain large amounts of potentially redundant data' 对应\"含大量可能冗余的数据\"。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-raw-image-format",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-c499a5131665",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 326
        }
      ],
      "independence": {
        "group_id": "raw-definition",
        "basis": []
      }
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "raw-sensor-data",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-raw-image-format",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-a67ba30f551a"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-a67ba30f551a",
          "exact": "Raw files thus contain the full dynamic range (typically 12- or 14-bit) data as read out from each of the camera's image sensor pixels."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-a67ba30f551a",
          "subject": "raw files",
          "predicate": "contain",
          "object": "full dynamic range (typically 12- or 14-bit) data as read out from each image sensor pixel"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002",
        "ARC-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "evidence-a67ba30f551a [0,134) 与 claim 完全对应：'the full dynamic range (typically 12- or 14-bit) data as read out from each of the camera's image sensor pixels' 即\"传感器每个像素读出的完整动态范围（通常 12 或 14 位）数据\"，full/typically 12- or 14-bit/each pixel 等限定与 claim 一致。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-raw-image-format",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-a67ba30f551a",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 134
        }
      ],
      "independence": {
        "group_id": "raw-sensor-data",
        "basis": []
      }
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "raw-cfa",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-raw-image-format",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-e17f2ae0d40a"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-e17f2ae0d40a",
          "exact": "The camera's sensor is almost invariably overlaid with a color filter array (CFA), usually a Bayer filter, consisting of a mosaic of a 2x2 matrix of red, green, blue and (second) green filters."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-e17f2ae0d40a",
          "subject": "camera sensor",
          "predicate": "is overlaid with",
          "object": "a color filter array (CFA), usually a Bayer filter, a mosaic of a 2x2 matrix of red, green, blue and (second) green filters"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002",
        "ARC-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "evidence-e17f2ae0d40a [0,177) 完整支撑 claim：'almost invariably overlaid with a color filter array (CFA), usually a Bayer filter' 对应\"几乎都覆有滤色阵列（CFA，通常是 Bayer 滤色阵）\"；'a mosaic of a 2x2 matrix of red, green, blue and (second) green filters' 对应\"由 2×2 红/绿/蓝/（第二个）绿滤镜构成的马赛克\"，与 claim 逐项一致。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
